+## Testing strategy
+
+RAGTree needs tests across the library core, current experiments, and optional integrations.
+
+| Test layer | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| Unit tests | Validate schemas, normalization, metrics, config loading, and utility functions. |
+| Protocol tests | Ensure adapters satisfy the expected interface. |
+| Smoke tests | Verify imports, CLI help, and minimal demo execution. |
+| Regression tests | Compare small fixed gold/prediction fixtures to expected metrics. |
+| Integration tests | Run optional adapters such as Chroma, Qdrant, Neo4j, FastAPI, and Streamlit behind opt-in markers. |
+| Experiment tests | Confirm existing scripts keep producing compatible JSONL outputs. |
+| Docker tests | Build the image and run `ragtree doctor` inside the container. |
+
+Recommended markers:
+
+```bash
+pytest -m "not integration"
+pytest -m neo4j
+pytest -m api
+pytest -m ui
+pytest -m docker
+```
