+```bash
+docker build -t ragtree:local .
+docker run --rm ragtree:local ragtree doctor
+```
+
+A local integration stack can later include:
+
+- RAGTree API service;
+- Streamlit workbench;
+- Neo4j;
+- Qdrant or Chroma persistence;
+- mounted datasets and output artifacts.
+
+---
+
+## Compatibility promise
+
+The transition toward a cleaner package should preserve current work.
+
+- Existing datasets should remain loadable.
+- Existing scripts should keep working or receive equivalent wrappers.
+- Existing output fields such as `id`, `document_id`, `type`, `relations`, and `pred_relations` should remain valid.
+- Existing evaluation outputs should remain comparable.
+- Current method names should remain visible in reports.
+- Notebooks should be converted progressively into smoke tests, examples, or documentation.
+
+---
+
+## Roadmap
+
+| Phase | Goal | Outcome |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | Identity and packaging reset | README, design document, icon, optional extras, installable CLI skeleton |
+| 1 | Core stabilization | Schemas, protocols, config, imports, doctor command, base tests |
+| 2 | Adapter layer | LLM, embeddings, vector stores, Neo4j, RDF, FastAPI, Streamlit behind extras |
+| 3 | Experiment preservation | Existing scripts wrapped with stable commands and run manifests |
+| 4 | True RAG demo | Minimal QA / evidence-grounded generation demo independent of relation extraction |
+| 5 | Integration tests | Optional test markers for Neo4j, API, UI, Docker, vector stores |
+| 6 | Alpha release | Tag, changelog, CI, docs, installation matrix, portfolio-ready examples |
